<rss version="2.0"><channel><title>PAT-HOT · P量子信息与计算</title><link>https://sun-zihang.github.io/pat-hot/#/all</link><description>量子信息与计算</description><lastBuildDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:41:13 GMT</lastBuildDate><item><title>Physicist develops detector capable of counting photons for quantum computing</title><link>https://phys.org/news/2026-11-physicist-detector-capable-photons-quantum.html</link><description>Detecting a single photon is a challenge in itself. But what if you also want to know exactly how many photons arrive at a particular point at the same time? Physicist Erik Baalbergen is working on light detectors that can do just that. They form a key building block for the optical quantum computer of the future.</description><guid isPermaLink="false">e25292964c3b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:41:13 GMT</pubDate><source>Phys.org 物理新闻</source><category>量子信息与计算</category></item><item><title>Ultrafast single-qubit gates through multi-photon transition removal</title><link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78373-4</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">4e7e23d911e8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:41:13 GMT</pubDate><source>Nature 量子物理</source><category>量子信息与计算</category></item><item><title>Enhancing bosonic qubit protection by squeezing</title><link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78025-7</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">516e5ade381d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:41:13 GMT</pubDate><source>Nature 量子物理</source><category>量子信息与计算</category></item><item><title>Particle collisions on a quantum computer</title><link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03490-2</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">75fdfb5c412f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:41:13 GMT</pubDate><source>Nature 量子物理</source><category>量子信息与计算</category></item><item><title>Beating the break-even point with autonomous quantum error correction</title><link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03486-